<title>SINGAPORE: TAIWAN TENDERS TO BUY UP TO 7,000/T OCTOBER MTBE.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN TENDERS TO BUY UP TO 7,000/T OCTOBER MTBE.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has tendered to buy 3,500 to 7,000-tonnes of methyl tertiary butyl ether (MTBE) for delivery October 1-20 to Kaohsiung or Keelung, a CPC official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender for the gasoline octane enhancer, closes August 19 and is valid for two days.</p>
<p>Its last spot tender award, for two 3,500-tonnes cargoes for September 6-20 delivery, was awarded to two producers at around $290 per tonne on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
